/* GNU ld version script for the public LibreSCRS_*.so libraries.
 * Whitelists LM-public C++ namespaces; everything else (bundled OpenSSL,
 * libresign internals, vendored nlohmann/miniz/pugixml, std-template
 * instantiations on internal types) collapses to local linkage.
 * See lib/LibreSCRS/CMakeLists.txt for full rationale.
 *
 * Syntax: GNU ld 2.46 — `extern "C++"` block matches against demangled
 * names. UNQUOTED patterns are glob wildcards (shell-style); DOUBLE-
 * QUOTED patterns are LITERAL matches with NO wildcard interpretation
 * (binutils `ld` info, §3.9 VERSION). Unquoted patterns cannot contain
 * spaces, which forces the leading-wildcard `*LibreSCRS::*` idiom: it
 * is the only single-line glob that simultaneously matches
 *     `LibreSCRS::Foo::bar(...)`
 * and the Itanium-ABI artefacts
 *     `typeinfo for LibreSCRS::Foo`
 *     `vtable for LibreSCRS::Foo`
 *     `VTT for LibreSCRS::Foo`
 *     `construction vtable for LibreSCRS::Foo`
 * — all of which carry an internal space the linker grammar refuses
 * to accept in an unquoted pattern. Anchored quoted entries
 * (`"LibreSCRS::*"`, `"typeinfo for LibreSCRS::*"`) were attempted
 * and rejected: they are LITERAL matches per ld docs and match
 * nothing at runtime.
 *
 * Trade-off — IMPLEMENTABILITY-FORCED leading-wildcard surface:
 *   The leading-wildcard glob also promotes any symbol whose
 *   demangled name MENTIONS a `LibreSCRS::` type anywhere. Empirically
 *   this leaks:
 *     - `emrtd::crypto::performBAC(LibreSCRS::SmartCard::Internal::
 *       PCSCConnection&, ...)` and `performPACE(...)` (statically
 *       linked into LibreSCRS_SecureChannel.so via the EMRTDCrypto
 *       archive)
 *     - `libresign::Pkcs11Token::Pkcs11Token(..., LibreSCRS::Secure::
 *       Buffer const&, ...)` and `libresign::NativeSigningService::
 *       appendSigner(...)` (statically linked into
 *       LibreSCRS_Signing.so via the libresign archive)
 *     - STL template instantiations templated on
 *       `LibreSCRS::SmartCard::Internal::Monitor` (specifically
 *       `std::thread::_State_impl<...LibreSCRS::SmartCard::Internal::
 *       Monitor...>::_M_run()` and its destructors / typeinfo /
 *       vtable)
 *   All three classes were investigated for stripping via:
 *     (a) anonymous-version + named LM_4 block — REJECTED by GNU ld
 *         2.46 ("anonymous version tag cannot be combined with other
 *         version tags").
 *     (b) multiple named-version blocks (`_DENY` before LM_4) — DID
 *         NOT strip; named-version local: blocks do not override
 *         later named-version global: matches for equally-non-
 *         specific wildcards.
 *     (c) intra-block `local:` with `emrtd::*` / `libresign::*` /
 *         `smartcard::*` — DID NOT strip; intra-block GLOBAL
 *         wildcard wins over intra-block LOCAL wildcard at equal
 *         specificity in GNU ld.
 *     (d) `--exclude-libs libLibreSign.a` / `--exclude-libs
 *         libEMRTDCrypto.a` — REJECTED because the legitimately
 *         public `LibreSCRS::Signing::layoutVisualSignature` lives
 *         in libresign source.
 *   The leaked symbols are NOT security-critical: they are functions
 *   whose demangled names happen to mention `LibreSCRS::` types.
 *   They cannot be invoked via dlsym without prior knowledge of their
 *   mangled names, do not break abstract-base polymorphism, and do
 *   not expose any LM private API to third-party `.so` consumers
 *   (who would have to declare matching `emrtd::` / `libresign::` /
 *   `smartcard::` namespaces and depend on internal-header types to
 *   link against them — a far harder ABI break than any reasonable
 *   third-party consumer would commit to). The trade-off is accepted
 *   as the cost of GNU ld's grammar; if a future binutils release
 *   admits an anchored-glob-with-RTTI-coverage form, this file
 *   should be re-narrowed.
 *
 * Cross-`.so` ABI surface — INTENTIONAL Internal::/detail:: exports:
 *   The LibreSCRS::*::Internal:: namespace IS part of the SHARED-build
 *   ABI for cross-`.so` plugin reach and the test-helper archive.
 *   Specifically:
 *     - LibreSCRS::SmartCard::Internal::Monitor, PCSCScanProvider,
 *       PCSCConnection, APDUCommand, APDUResponse, MonitorEvent —
 *       required for plugin .so files and the test-helper archive to
 *       link against shared LibreSCRS_SmartCard.
 *     - LibreSCRS::SecureChannel::detail::ChannelStateMutator —
 *       required for SmartCard.so + emrtd-plugin.so to call
 *       SetCurrentApplet / ReplaceKeys.
 *     - LibreSCRS::SmartCard::Internal::HolderChannelAccessor —
 *       required for plugin .so files to obtain a channel pointer
 *       from a holder.
 *     - LibreSCRS::Trust::detail::TrustStoreInternalAccess::
 *       mergeTrustedListAnchors — required for Signing.so to merge
 *       anchors into Trust.so's store.
 *     - LibreSCRS::Trust::detail::TrustAnchorProvider typeinfo —
 *       required for cross-`.so` dynamic_cast on subclasses linked in
 *       different .so files.
 *     - LibreSCRS::Certificate::detail::lookupOidName — required for
 *       the OidDatabase test which links against the SHARED
 *       LibreSCRS_Certificate.
 *   Third-party consumers MUST NOT rely on Internal:: or detail::
 *   symbols; both are unstable across minor releases and are exported
 *   only because the shared-build link graph mechanically requires
 *   it.
 */

LM_4 {
    global:
        extern "C++" {
            /* Wildcard prefix matches both bare names
             *     `LibreSCRS::Foo::bar(...)`
             * and Itanium-ABI RTTI / vtable artefacts demangled as
             *     `typeinfo for LibreSCRS::Foo`
             *     `typeinfo name for LibreSCRS::Foo`
             *     `vtable for LibreSCRS::Foo`
             *     `VTT for LibreSCRS::Foo`
             *     `construction vtable for LibreSCRS::Foo`
             * which are required for cross-SO polymorphism
             * (dynamic_cast, exception catch, vtable lookup of public
             * abstract bases such as `ISecureChannel`). A bare
             * `LibreSCRS::*` glob misses the `... for LibreSCRS::*`
             * forms and silently demotes class-level visibility to
             * LOCAL in the .so, breaking link of consumers that
             * downcast or instantiate the type. See the file-header
             * "Trade-off" block for the IMPLEMENTABILITY-FORCED side
             * of this glob and the four narrowing approaches GNU ld
             * 2.46 grammar rejected. */
            *LibreSCRS::*;
        };
    local:
        /* Strip test-only injection helpers from the dynamic export
         * set. The `*LibreSCRS::*` global glob above would otherwise
         * authoritatively override the per-declaration
         * `LIBRESCRS_INTERNAL` hidden-visibility attribute and leak
         * these dlsym-reachable footguns into the production shared
         * library, defeating the documented runtime hardening of
         * `LibreSCRS::SmartCard::MonitorService::SubscriptionId`
         * (privatised raw-int ctor) and of
         * `LibreSCRS::SmartCard::CardSession`'s channel install path.
         *
         * The helper bodies live in the build-tree-only
         * `LibreSCRS_SmartCard_TestHelpers` archive: test executables
         * that need them link the archive alongside the production
         * target, so the symbols enter the test executable directly
         * and never need to be found in the .so at link time.
         *
         * Note: the broader `*LibreSCRS::*::detail::*` glob would
         * also be sound, but it would strip the legitimate
         * cross-`.so` plugin-reach detail helpers (e.g.
         * `SecureChannel::detail::ChannelStateMutator`,
         * `SmartCard::detail::PcscBridge::unwrap`,
         * `Certificate::detail::lookupOidName`,
         * `Signing::detail::translatePublicRequestToLibresign`,
         * `Trust::detail::TrustAnchorProvider`,
         * `Trust::detail::TrustStoreInternalAccess`,
         * `SmartCard::detail::sessionGeneration`,
         * `SmartCard::detail::makeDetachedCardSession`), each of
         * which is consumed by either a card plugin or a sibling
         * `LibreSCRS_*.so` via the `DT_NEEDED` edge.
         *
         * The narrow per-symbol list captures only the three
         * test-injection footguns plus the `MonitorFactory` friend
         * bridge they go through. */
        extern "C++" {
            *LibreSCRS::SmartCard::detail::makeMonitorWithProvider*;
            *LibreSCRS::SmartCard::detail::makeSubscriptionIdForTest*;
            *LibreSCRS::SmartCard::detail::MonitorFactory*;
            *LibreSCRS::SmartCard::detail::ChannelInjector::installForTesting*;
        };
        *;
};
